Python and uv

Install:
  Install missing uv and Python; create missing default command links for uv-managed Python.

Upgrade:
  Update installed uv and uv-managed Python versions.

Status:
  Report uv and Python command locations and versions, and locally detected Python installations.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  Missing uv is installed in ~/.local/bin; Python versions and command links are managed by uv.
  Existing python/python3 entries in the uv command directory are preserved; upgrade updates uv-managed Python versions.
  CLI tools such as ruff and pre-commit belong to the tools module.
  Open a new terminal after installation to load environment changes.
